   "props": {
    "title": "Command, in one breath",
    "items": [
     "Button handlers did the work and vanished, so undo needed mirrored switches and hand-stashed data.",
     "A request should be an object that carries how to do AND undo it, with the data it needs inside.",
     "Command: invoker runs and stores command objects; each reverses itself. New action, new command."
    ],
    "challenge": "A design tool needs multi-level undo, plus the ability to record a sequence of edits and replay it as a one-click macro.",
    "question": "Does Command fit? What's the command, and who is the invoker?",
    "dur": 51.043
   }
